' plan-116-I: a `canvas::DrawItem` cannot cross a thread's DATA plane, because two of
' its variants now carry a resource.
'
' This is a DELIBERATE narrowing and the fixture exists to pin it. Before this letter,
' `Picture.image` and `Text.font` were `ImageRef`/`FontRef` records holding a plain
' `Integer`, so a list of `DrawItem` slipped across a data plane with nothing to object
' to -- and what arrived on the other side was an id whose resource the sending thread
' still owned. The type system could not see that; it can now.
'
' The remedy the message names is the right one: move the `Image`/`Font` on the RES
' plane and build the scene on the receiving side.
'
' The message names `RES canvas.Image` rather than the font: `DrawItem` is a union and
' the cause walk reports the FIRST resource-carrying variant it reaches, which is
' `Picture.image`. Both variants carry one, and either alone would be enough to refuse
' the plane -- so do not "fix" this fixture by removing whichever one looks unused.
IMPORT canvas
IMPORT io
IMPORT thread

' The message plane: a data plane, so a resource inside `DrawItem` is a plane mix-up
' with a nameable remedy.
FUNC viaMessage(t AS Thread OF List OF canvas::DrawItem TO Integer) AS Integer
  RETURN 0
END FUNC

' The output plane is a data plane too, and must report identically.
FUNC viaOutput(t AS Thread OF Integer TO List OF canvas::DrawItem) AS Integer
  RETURN 0
END FUNC

FUNC main AS Integer
  io::print("unreachable")
  RETURN 0
END FUNC
